   "source": [
    "# Pricing and Hedging of European Options\n",
    "Anas KHAYAR",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from math import comb\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 3: Cox Ross Rubinstein Model\n",
    "\n",
    "Discrete model on N time steps $t_0=0 < t_1 < \\dots < t_N=T$, with $\\delta = T/N$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Riskless asset: $(1+r_N)^i$ at time $t_i$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Risky asset: $S^{(N)}_{t_i} = T^{(N)}_i S^{(N)}_{t_{i-1}}$, where $T^{(N)}_i \\in \\{1+h_N, 1+b_N\\}$, i.i.d., with $b_N < r_N < h_N$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Discounted price: $\\tilde S^{(N)}_{t_i} = S^{(N)}_{t_i}/(1+r_N)^i$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Risk neutral probability $Q$: the probability under which $(\\tilde S^{(N)}_{t_i})_i$ is a martingale.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Question 1\n",
    "Find $q_N = Q(T_1^{(N)} = 1+h_N)$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Condition: $E_Q[T_1^{(N)}] = 1+r_N$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer:\n",
    "$$q_N = \\frac{r_N - b_N}{h_N - b_N}$$\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Question 2 (0.5/20)\n",
    "Express $Prix^{(N)} = \\dfrac{1}{(1+r_N)^N}E_Q[f(S^{(N)}_{t_N})]$ using $r_N, q_N, s, h_N, b_N, f$, as a sum with binomial coefficients.\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer:\n",
    "$$Prix^{(N)} = \\frac{1}{(1+r_N)^N}\\sum_{k=0}^{N} \\binom{N}{k} q_N^k (1-q_N)^{N-k} f\\left(s(1+h_N)^k(1+b_N)^{N-k}\\right)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$k$ is the number of up moves among the N time steps.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Question 3 (2/20): First pricer\n",
    "Implement `price1(N, rN, hN, bN, s, f)` returning $Prix^{(N)}$ from Q2.\n",
    "\n",
    "Use `math.comb(N, k)` for the binomial coefficient, sum over `k` from 0 to N.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import math\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def price1(N, rN, hN, bN, s, f):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Calculate the price of a European call option using the binomial model.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Parameters:\n",
    "    N (int): Number of time steps\n",
    "    rN (float): Risk-free interest rate per time step\n",
    "    hN (float): Up factor per time step\n",
    "    bN (float): Down factor per time step\n",
    "    s (float): Current stock price\n",
    "    f (float): Strike price\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "    float: Price of the European call option\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Calculate the risk-neutral probability\n",
    "    qn = (rN - bN) / (hN - bN)\n",
    "    sum = 0.0 \n",
    "    for k in range (N+1) :\n",
    "        ST = s * (1+hN)**k * (1+bN)**(N-k)  # Stock price at maturity\n",
    "        proba_k = qn ** k * (1-qn) ** (N-k)\n",
    "        proba_total = proba_k * math.comb(N,k)  # Binomial coefficient\n",
    "        sum += proba_total * f(ST)  # Payoff function for a call option\n",
    "    price = sum / (1 + rN) ** N  # Discount back to present value\n",
    "    return price\n",
    "    \n",
    "    \n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
